{"route":"/docs/5.2/helpers/ratio/","version":"5.2","renderedVersion":"5.2","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Ratios","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use generated pseudo elements to make an element maintain the aspect ratio of your choosing. Perfect for responsively handling video or slideshow embeds based on the width of the parent."},"blocks":[{"id":"about","type":"heading","en":"About","level":2},{"id":"about--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use the ratio helper to manage the aspect ratios of external content like <code>&lt;iframe&gt;</code>s, <code>&lt;embed&gt;</code>s, <code>&lt;video&gt;</code>s, and <code>&lt;object&gt;</code>s. These helpers also can be used on any standard HTML child element (e.g., a <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>). Styles are applied from the parent <code>.ratio</code> class directly to the child."},{"id":"about--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Aspect ratios are declared in a Sass map and included in each class via CSS variable, which also allows <a href=\"#custom-ratios\">custom aspect ratios</a>."},{"id":"about--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"about--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>Pro-Tip!</strong> You don’t need <code>frameborder=&quot;0&quot;</code> on your <code>&lt;iframe&gt;</code>s as we override that for you in <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/content/reboot/\">Reboot</a>."}]},{"id":"example","type":"heading","en":"Example","level":2},{"id":"example--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Wrap any embed, like an <code>&lt;iframe&gt;</code>, in a parent element with <code>.ratio</code> and an aspect ratio class. The immediate child element is automatically sized thanks to our universal selector <code>.ratio &gt; *</code>."},{"id":"example--example-1","type":"demo","key":"a78e820f854397f60adb","height":300},{"id":"example--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"ratio ratio-16x9\">\n  <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/zpOULjyy-n8?rel=0\" title=\"YouTube video\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"aspect-ratios","type":"heading","en":"Aspect ratios","level":2},{"id":"aspect-ratios--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Aspect ratios can be customized with modifier classes. By default the following ratio classes are provided:"},{"id":"aspect-ratios--example-1","type":"demo","key":"eca09a2443416354db45","height":300},{"id":"aspect-ratios--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"ratio ratio-1x1\">\n  <div>1x1</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ratio ratio-4x3\">\n  <div>4x3</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ratio ratio-16x9\">\n  <div>16x9</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ratio ratio-21x9\">\n  <div>21x9</div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"custom-ratios","type":"heading","en":"Custom ratios","level":2},{"id":"custom-ratios--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Each <code>.ratio-*</code> class includes a CSS custom property (or CSS variable) in the selector. You can override this CSS variable to create custom aspect ratios on the fly with some quick math on your part."},{"id":"custom-ratios--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"For example, to create a 2x1 aspect ratio, set <code>--bs-aspect-ratio: 50%</code> on the <code>.ratio</code>."},{"id":"custom-ratios--example-1","type":"demo","key":"6cce96a6f2b0c48ec279","height":300},{"id":"custom-ratios--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"ratio\" style=\"--bs-aspect-ratio: 50%;\">\n  <div>2x1</div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"custom-ratios--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"This CSS variable makes it easy to modify the aspect ratio across breakpoints. The following is 4x3 to start, but changes to a custom 2x1 at the medium breakpoint."},{"id":"custom-ratios--code-2","type":"code","value":".ratio-4x3 {\n  @include media-breakpoint-up(md) {\n    --bs-aspect-ratio: 50%; // 2x1\n  }\n}","language":"scss"},{"id":"custom-ratios--example-2","type":"demo","key":"cfb6a53e38cd6dbd4cf9","height":300},{"id":"custom-ratios--code-3","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"ratio ratio-4x3\">\n  <div>4x3, then 2x1</div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"sass-map","type":"heading","en":"Sass map","level":2},{"id":"sass-map--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Within <code>_variables.scss</code>, you can change the aspect ratios you want to use. Here’s our default <code>$ratio-aspect-ratios</code> map. Modify the map as you like and recompile your Sass to put them to use."},{"id":"sass-map--code-1","type":"code","value":"$aspect-ratios: (\n  \"1x1\": 100%,\n  \"4x3\": calc(3 / 4 * 100%),\n  \"16x9\": calc(9 / 16 * 100%),\n  \"21x9\": calc(9 / 21 * 100%)\n);","language":"scss"}],"demos":[{"key":"a78e820f854397f60adb","html":"\n<div class=\"ratio ratio-16x9\">\n  <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/zpOULjyy-n8?rel=0\" title=\"YouTube video\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"eca09a2443416354db45","html":"\n<div class=\"ratio ratio-1x1\">\n  <div>1x1</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ratio ratio-4x3\">\n  <div>4x3</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ratio ratio-16x9\">\n  <div>16x9</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ratio ratio-21x9\">\n  <div>21x9</div>\n</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example bd-example-ratios"},"sprite":""},{"key":"6cce96a6f2b0c48ec279","html":"\n<div class=\"ratio\" style=\"--bs-aspect-ratio: 50%;\">\n  <div>2x1</div>\n</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example bd-example-ratios"},"sprite":""},{"key":"cfb6a53e38cd6dbd4cf9","html":"\n<div class=\"ratio ratio-4x3\">\n  <div>4x3, then 2x1</div>\n</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example bd-example-ratios bd-example-ratios-breakpoint"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","hr